{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:3", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "3", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The Buddhist, Naiyāyika, Sāṃkhya, Jaina, Vaiśeṣika and Jaiminīya — these are the names of the darśanas.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-views-of-other-darsanas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:45-58", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "45-58", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "In the Jaina darśana the deity is the Jina, free of attachment and aversion; the realities are soul, non-soul, merit, demerit, inflow, stopping, bondage, shedding and liberation; the means of knowledge are direct and indirect; and a thing is many-sided.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-tattvas", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Section range recalled.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:77-78", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "77-78", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Some hold Nyāya and Vaiśeṣika to be one; for them the Lokāyata makes up the sixth darśana.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-views-of-other-darsanas"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:80", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "80"}, "paraphrase": "The Lokāyatas say: there is no soul, no release (nirvṛti); merit and demerit do not exist, nor the fruit of good and evil deeds.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:paraloka-denial"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Haribhadra (Jain doxography). Verse number from memory.", "coverage": ["B1"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:81", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "81"}, "paraphrase": "'This world is only as much as falls within the range of the senses; see, my dear, the wolf's footprint of which the unlearned speak' — the ignorant are misled by what the learned claim, as by wolf-tracks faked in the dust.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:vrkapada"], "concepts": ["cpt:pratyaksa-only", "cpt:vrkapada-parable"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Haribhadra (Jain doxography). Verse number and wording from memory; the same verse (with puruṣa for loka) is quoted in Candrakīrti's Prasannapadā on MMK 18.6 (checked in a local e-text with OCR errors). The parable is told by Guṇaratna.", "coverage": ["B1"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:82", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "82"}, "paraphrase": "'Drink and eat, O fair-eyed one; what is past, O shapely one, is not yours; what has gone, timid one, does not return; this body is only an aggregate.'", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["ethics", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:carvaka-hedonism"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Haribhadra (Jain doxography). Verse number from memory.", "coverage": ["B1"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra:83-85", "source": "src:saddarsanasamuccaya-haribhadra", "location": {"ref": "83-85"}, "paraphrase": "Earth, water, fire and air are the four elements, the ground of consciousness; the means of knowledge is the senses alone; from the combination of the elements arise body and the rest, and the self (consciousness) is established as intoxicating power arises from the ingredients of liquor.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:bhuta-caitanya", "cpt:pratyaksa-only"], "teachers": ["tch:haribhadra"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "Reported by an opponent: Haribhadra (Jain doxography). Verse numbers and exact content from memory.", "coverage": ["B1"], "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
